                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[i]Dead of Night[/i] reminds me those weird adventure games that you would find on old computers (not something you see a lot these days). Gameplay can be vaguely described as exploration game with elements of surviving and stealth. You have to look for items hidden around the map and match them to correct puzzles. Although I think it relies a lot on nostalgia so it is a little clunky because of it. The game had some issues but most of them have been fixed. I finally decided to rewrite this review because the developer has been doing constant updates and supported the game despite poor sales.\n\nYou play as a vampire who can roam at night but must hide during a day. There is a day/night system which you will need to pay attention to. If you get killed by any means other than Sun you simply respawn next to your castle where you can regain your strength. When you kill people you might get a key to the store and then have to figure out where the heck you have to go. The puzzles can be a little difficult but I think that is part of what made those games special. You can also turn into a human for a limited time which allows you to move undetected.There is some forced backtracking especially if you get killed by the sun. \n\nPixel art is decent in regards to what this game is going for. Still, I think some of the areas are too generic and there should be more variety. The swamp area looks really dull for example and those immortal animals that attack you are so annoying. Also, some of the music choices are a little off (like the town theme). Each area needs its own soundtrack.Perhaps the best part of the game is the sense of humor. Just the idea of you being a vampire running in and out of your castle is fun. Some of the events and puzzle solutions were hilarious.\n\n[h1] Final Thoughts: 7/10 [/h1] \n\nAfter couple recent updates I can finally recommend the game with confidence.  If you ever played those clunky adventures for old systems I think you will find this nostalgic. It is a very faithful retro game so I hope it will find more audience.\n\n[code]For more hidden gems:\nhttp://store.steampowered.com/curator/31294838-Hidden-Gem-Discovery/[/code]",
